# <Project>: Agent Rules

> Lean, always-loaded. Only rules that change agent behavior. For each line ask:
> "would removing this cause a mistake?" If not, cut it or move it to a skill.

## Before every session
Read: this file, then `specs/<active-feature>/spec.md` and `tasks.md`, then `DECISIONS.md`.
Confirm the active task matches what you're about to do; if not, stop and ask.

## Identity & taboos
- <What this is, who it's for, commercial status.>
- Never mention AI tooling/automation in shipped code, comments, commits, or docs.
- Never use the restricted term "<X>" anywhere that ships. This is a contractual naming
  restriction, not a style preference. A test greps the source for it.

## Hard rules
- <Stack constraint, for example vanilla JS, no frameworks.>
- Smallest safe change only. Do not refactor unrelated code.
- Read before writing. Do not rewrite working logic.
- Secrets: `<KEY>` only in serverless functions. Only `<PUBLIC_KEY>` may appear client-side.

## Workflow
- Per feature: spec, then plan, then tasks, then implement (TDD), then review, then ship.
- Tests first. A step is not done until the suite is green AND you have shown the output.
- After each step: update `DECISIONS.md` (rationale) and the spec status.

## Commits
- Conventional prefixes: feat / fix / refactor / chore / test / security.
- No mention of AI/automation in messages.

## Pointers (loaded on demand, not every turn)
- Architecture & durable UI conventions: @ARCHITECTURE.md
- Test commands & conventions: @TESTING.md
